<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_SMG_T1">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type82_SMG_</defName>
		<label>Type 82 SMG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 9x18mm Makarov. 15-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 82 is a Chinese copy of the Polish PM-63 Rak SMG developed in the 1980s. PM-63 SMGs captured from Vietnamese forces during the Sino-Vietnamese border conflict were liked by the Chinese forces that had them, as the PLA at the time had no SMG that was as light or compact; the PLA instead used full-sized SMGs chambered in 7.62 Tokarev. Thus, the PM-63 was reverse engineered and a near-identical copy was produced. It is not known how long the Type 82 was produced or remained in Chinese military service for, but it has since been superceded by more modern designs.</description>
